//! Application state and event loop.
//!
//! `App` groups the live state of the program (prompt buffer, output
//! buffer, stream channel, conversation history) and owns the async
//! event loop. Splitting state from rendering (`view.rs`) and from
//! key predicates (`shortcuts.rs`) keeps this file focused on
//! dispatch: "what changes in response to which event."
//!
//! `App`'s fields are `pub(crate)` so the renderer (`view.rs`) can
//! read them directly without per-field accessors whose only job is
//! to satisfy encapsulation. The shannon-tui crate is the only thing
//! that can see them.
//!
//! The loop is event-driven, not polled. `tokio::select!` waits on
//! crossterm's `EventStream` and the streamed-stub channel
//! simultaneously; nothing happens between events. There is no idle
//! tick — the perf ambition (thousands of FPS when work is to be
//! done) is served better by zero work when there is none.
//!
//! `Backend` lives in `shannon-core`. The TUI does not know whether
//! it is talking to a canned stub or the real Anthropic API; both
//! produce `StreamMsg` over the same channel.

